# Gate and identifier antipatterns (agents)

Cursor agents editing Idol source or gates **must not** mint compound binding
names, mashed selector kingdoms, or law-violating identifiers.

## Forbidden gate compounds (convicted on added lines)

Never introduce these binding names — `gate/idiom.id` rejects them:

```text
scandiff scanline diffhead bareend stagelist pluralpath pluralfix
nativebackend backendnative
machinery machinerycall machinerypeek inferstrhole
worlddot qualworlddot ingressonly rungate writetemp pathbody treebody
viewrouter viewproof ingestbody graphbody …
```

## Required decomposition

| Wrong | Right |
|---|---|
| `nativebackend`, `backendnative` | `backend/native` home hierarchy |
| `pluralpath(home)` | `list(staged)(body)` + inline `plural(root(line))` |
| `stagelist(body)` | `list(staged)(body)` |
| `machinery(name)` | `collision(name)` + `flag(..., "router(", ...)` rows |
| `scandiff` | `scan(diff)(body)` or `feed(body)` |

## Forbidden identifiers (any new binding or path component)

One lowercase word per binding. Reject via `gate/idiom.id` (`eq`, `term`) and
`gate/path.id` (`verdict`, `walk`, `sep`, `mash`, `plural`):

- snake_case, camelCase, kebab-case, numeric taxonomy suffixes
- `*able`/`*ible` protocol names (`readable`, `callable`, `invokable`, …)
- collision identities (`router`, `gateway`, `registry`, `context`, …)
- codec machinery (`codec`, `encoder`, `decoder`, `converter`, …)
- plural roots on **new staged paths** (`scripts/`, `examples/`, …) — rehome per
  `docs/spec/path-migration.md` / GAP-168

## Before editing gates

Read `AGENTS.md` § Gate scan boundaries. Match existing phase owners: `lex`,
`face`, `realm`, `term`, `deny`, `edge`, `home`, `adj`, `walk`, `verdict`,
`list(staged)`, `list(tree)`, `feed`, `control`.

Do not add a second gate ontology to classify law — extend `flag()` rows and
one-word helpers only.
